## Dataset Characteristics \& Variable Dictionary ($N = 303$)

The final analytical sample ($N = 303$) reflects verified responses collected between 10 March and 15 April 2026:

* **Demographics:** Female: 215 ($70.96%$), Male: 88 ($29.04%$).
* **Professional Categories:** Undergraduate Students ($n = 224, 73.93%$), Academic/Graduate Researchers ($n = 54, 17.82%$), Licensed Practicing Pharmacists ($n = 25, 8.25%$).
* **Experience Levels:** $<1$ year ($26.40%$), 1–5 years ($50.50%$), 6–10 years ($14.85%$), $>10$ years ($8.25%$).

### Core Construct Specifications (Formative Composite Indices, 0–100 Scale)

* `PILS\_pct`: Pharmaceutical IP Literacy Score (9 objective binary legal items, Mean = $38.87 \\pm 15.55%$, Median = $44.44%$).
* `IAI\_pct`: Intellectual Property Attitude Index (10 Likert items, Mean = $71.30 \\pm 8.27%$, Median = $72.50%$).
* `IRS\_pct`: Perceived Institutional Readiness Score (4 Likert items on TTOs, funding, legal support; Mean = $17.82 \\pm 20.35%$, $48.51%$ zeros).
* `IPI\_pct`: Innovation Practice Index (3 behavioral items on patents, R\&D, tech transfer; Mean = $10.45 \\pm 17.91%$, $71.95%$ zeros).
* `Diagnostic\_Gap`: Arithmetic difference ($\\text{IAI\_pct} - \\text{IPI\_pct}$, Mean = $60.84 \\pm 19.93$ points).

\---

## Instructions for Reproduction

To reproduce all tables, statistics, and regression models in the manuscript:

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/chadikhatib/innovation-capability-constraints.git
cd innovation-capability-constraints

# 2. Install required dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 3. Execute the reproducible statistical audit script
python reproducible\_statistical\_audit.py
```

